N5008 [temp.variadic]/5 + [expr.new]: instantiating a function template
whose BODY contains a new-initializer pack expansion over an EMPTY pack
(`::new((void*)__location) _Tp(static_cast<_Args&&>(__args)...)` with
_Args = {}) fails with "symbol '__args' is unknown" -- the drain's
per-element expander handles ordinary CALL argument lists (the plain
call sibling kernel passes) but not the new-initializer's expression
list.  Split from the round-112 investigation (the REQUIREMENT-side
empty-pack expansion is fixed; this is the body-side sibling).  The
walker in cpp_typecheck_method_bodies.cpp ~745 (`is_arg_list`) and the
N==0 path of cpp_instantiate_template.cpp are the places to look; a
first attempt that mirrored the function-call branch inside
cpp_instantiate_template's expanded_names walker was NOT REACHED for
this shape (probe confirmed) and was reverted.
Runtime-verified g++ 13 / clang++ 18 (placement-new definition supplied
in the harness).
